==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|werden|wërden|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|werdan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*werþaną}}. Cognate with Dutch {{term|worden|lang=nl}}, Swedish {{term|varda|lang=sv}} and obsolete English verb {{term|worth||to become|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-werden.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|/ˈvɛɐ̯dn̩/|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-irregular|wird|wurde|geworden|past participle 2=worden|auxiliary=sein}}

# {{context|auxiliary|with an infinitive|past participle {{term|geworden|lang=de}}|lang=de}} [[will]]; to be going (to do something); {{non-gloss definition|forms the future tense}}
#: ''Ich '''werde''' nach Hause gehen.'' 
#:: I '''will''' go home.
# {{context|auxiliary|with a past participle|past participle {{term|worden|lang=de}}|lang=de}} to be done; {{non-gloss definition|forms the passive voice}}
#: ''Das Buch '''wird''' gerade gelesen. (present tense)''
#:: The book is '''being''' read.
#: ''Er war geschlagen '''worden'''. (past perfect tense)''
#:: He had '''been''' beaten.
# {{context|intransitive|past participle: “[[geworden]]”|lang=de}} to [[become]]; to [[get]]; to [[grow]]; to [[turn]]
#: ''Es '''wird''' heißer.''
#:: It's '''getting''' hotter.

